five four three two one and liftoff of  the space shuttle Discovery with the  Hubble Space Telescope our window on the  universe Hubble is the first major  optical telescope sent into space taking  images from above the distortion of the  atmosphere and light pollution nASA has  called it the ultimate mountaintop when  the possibility of a telescope in space  opened up  astronomers jumped on the idea  scientists have used Hubble to observe  the most distant stars and galaxies as  well as the planets in our solar system  it's most famous photo was taken in 1995  a so-called Deep Field image showing  areas of the universe as they were  billions of years ago during three  decades in orbit Hubble has influenced  many people back on earth it's my job to  make things up for a living and  constantly use my imagination but Hubble  and the dedicated scientists behind it  take all of that a step further I've  been fortunate to work on shows like the  Orville battlestar galactica I spent  almost two decades on Star Trek our  space is kind of my game but you know  when you look at the vistas that have  been gifted to us by Hubble it changes  not just your mind but it changes your  DNA Hubble orbits the earth once every  hour and a half giving us a great  witness in space Hubble was also the  first telescope designed to be visited  in space so astronauts could carry out  repairs but early in its mission  engineers found a problem that shocked  them the images sent back to earth were  blurred a lot of people feel we don't  need the Star Wars defense system  anymore hey I think we should keep it  you know if only to shoot down that  Hubble spacecraft put this thing out of  its misery  after twelve years of construction at a  cost of billions of dollars astronauts  were sent to space in 1993 to fix the  faulty lens that mission was a success  and fantastic images began to be  transmitted back to earth when people  talk about the legacy of Hubble I I  think among its greatest legacies will  be helping humanity understand that yeah  when things go to space we can in fact  they're not it's not hopeless if there's  something wrong we can service them in  in many cases if we make some  preparation to do that but Hubble does  have an expiry date scientists estimate  it should last another five years or  until its solar batteries stopped  working until then Hubble can build on  its legacy revealing yet more images  from far depths of our universe Lea  Harding al-jazeera
 

